[{"id":213,"url":"http://127.0.0.1:3001/recovery-admin/glantri-app/pulls/487","number":487,"user":{"id":3,"login":"glantri-builder","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"glantri-builder@noreply.127.0.0.1","avatar_url":"http://127.0.0.1:3001/avatars/0c82a6d630cb8db2a77c0779776645f8","html_url":"http://127.0.0.1:3001/glantri-builder","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2026-09-06T12:08:26Z","restricted":true,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"limited","followers_count":0,"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":0,"username":"glantri-builder"},"title":"WIP: S7 Round End Review chronology, navigation, and modifier corrections (#481)","body":"Closes the Builder portion of #481, S7 Wave 3 Lane A. This branch is from frozen `dev` `370efeb15eff232109ea095e8156d60e439ad674`; head `3a23de6a63768701ac91c5c46f870ed3817f023c` (repair child of `de3cfe31e7563d936d48c70db70ee6b8e5e0ae7f`). Built in a visible ChatGPT Work / Codex Builder session with the repository execution identity `glantri-builder \u003cglantri-builder@localhost\u003e`. Draft for independent QA and integration; do not merge as a Builder acceptance.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- **(a) Terminal vocabulary:** T1/T2/T3/T4/T6 now consume `isCombatGenericActionLive`; T5's terminal type derives from the status enum through the shared terminal values. A test iterates every declared status and checks helper/Set/opportunity agreement. T7's modifier transition legality table and T8's authorization table were inspected as reference twins; neither is in this edit scope. The separate `EncounterStatus` vocabulary was not conflated with generic action status.\n- **(b) Chronology:** the unpersisted Round End plan now presents, in this explicit order, **active timed effects → countdown/checkpoint and old/new duration → expirations → due checks/rolls → resulting state**, followed by participant GM Review and the explicit round boundary. GM and player views render the ordered moments. Health, effect, observation, and participant Review process order follows the same reading. This does not itself execute, accept, or commit a Review command.\n- **(c) Navigation:** the default GM Review sequence includes consequential participants; every combatant remains available through “Inspect any combatant” and the Combat Inspector. The plan still emits every participant stage and the active participant's task, including genuine no-work bookkeeping. `participantIds`, iteration, `activeParticipantId`, scheduler, authorization, the persisted SU cursor/status writers, and the `complete_round` gate remain unchanged. The existing `facts.deterministicNoWorkCompletion` marker labels a deterministically completed participant as bookkeeping, not as personally inspected by the GM. Only an explicit GM boundary action advances the step or round.\n- **(c2) Automatic-only consequence:** the `hasAutomatic` effect-review arm is now `human_decision`. A direct canonical-only duration decrement with no legacy proposal measured `required/human_decision`; before the change it measured `required/deterministic_transition`. The current fixed-duration producer also mirrors its tick to the legacy duration field, so this synthetic case establishes the projection guard without claiming that today's producer emits it unmirrored.\n- **(c3) Death timer:** a named test locks the due, unresolved `blocksReview:false` catastrophic requirement to `required/human_decision`, `legacy_incomplete`, and conditional participant completion.\n- **(d) Correction:** a GM can correct an already committed, active canonical round-duration decrement in the Inspector while the round is in Review. The route checks GM access, encounter and participant revisions, effect version, and the accepted committed proposal. It appends a canonical `update` transition with the existing `legacy_compatibility` reason and `gmOverride.reasonCode/userId`; `prior` survives. It adds no persisted field or enum member. The Encounter correction count is read from those transitions. The control remains available after the participant's SU step is complete, and the history survives reload. V1 correction is limited to active round-duration decrements; no damage, Health-roll, or distance correction carrier was added.\n- **Privacy:** player participant responses strip the entire raw `canonicalTransitions` array and project the public canonical lifecycle; GM reads and stored effects retain correction history. Player encounter commands explicitly project `commit_round_end_participant_review`: the controlled participant receives public outcome identifiers/status and effect IDs, while both `previousEffect` and `nextEffect` snapshots, `canonicalSuReview`, other private facts, and GM actor identity stay internal. Player Review DTOs still exclude another participant's Review and warnings internals. The broader command-helper default-path audit is #488.\n\n## Boundaries and overlap\n\nNo schema, Prisma migration, docs, `combatRoundStep.ts`, `combatModifierLifecycle.ts`, `scenarios.test.ts`, `localServiceClient.ts`, route-segment page/layout/config, or M1/M2 code changed. The diff in `combatHistoryProjection.ts` is one addition after old line 1220; it does **not** touch #451-owned lines 404–446. `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/dev` returned the frozen `370efeb1` immediately before the commit.\n\n## Repair-cycle verification at `3a23de6a63768701ac91c5c46f870ed3817f023c`\n\n- `pnpm typecheck`: 17/17 tasks passed. `pnpm lint`: 11/11 passed. `FORMAT_BASE_SHA=\"$(git merge-base origin/dev HEAD)\" pnpm format:check:changed`: echoed `370efeb15eff232109ea095e8156d60e439ad674`; 20 changed files passed. `git diff --check de3cfe31 HEAD`: passed.\n- `pnpm --filter @glantri/domain exec vitest run --no-file-parallelism`: 88 files / 1,533 passed. `pnpm --filter @glantri/web exec vitest run --no-file-parallelism`: 177 files / 1,541 passed / one skipped.\n- `pnpm db:task:setup --task 481-s7-repair-cycle1a3` and `pnpm db:task:migrate`: isolated database ready, 29 migrations applied. `pnpm db:task:exec -- pnpm --filter @glantri/api exec vitest run --no-file-parallelism`: 648 passed; one known unrelated `characters.targetValidation.integration.test.ts` failure (`Saved target Group must match its explicit definition`); one file skipped. The direct player `/my-participant`, player state-update, GM correction-history, and serialized player encounter assertions passed in the targeted route test (4/4).\n- `pnpm db:task:exec -- pnpm build`: 11/11 tasks passed. Full Playwright against the isolated built stack and complete task environment: **37 tests / 35 passed / 2 failed**. The S7 test passed; the same two baseline Artifact failures remain at `artifactImports.spec.ts:10` and `artifacts.spec.ts:16`. Frozen `dev` baseline previously measured independently: 36 / 34 / 2.\n\nThe repair is a Builder candidate for fresh independent floor-class QA. PR remains draft; no merge or self-acceptance.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":null,"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_reviewers_teams":[],"state":"open","draft":true,"is_locked":false,"comments":1,"review_comments":0,"additions":1898,"deletions":79,"changed_files":20,"html_url":"http://127.0.0.1:3001/recovery-admin/glantri-app/pulls/487","diff_url":"http://127.0.0.1:3001/recovery-admin/glantri-app/pulls/487.diff","patch_url":"http://127.0.0.1:3001/recovery-admin/glantri-app/pulls/487.patch","mergeable":false,"merged":false,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"merged_by":null,"allow_maintainer_edit":false,"base":{"label":"dev","ref":"dev","sha":"c9d3acc5f4e321eabcecabb5f3cebae56df87df5","repo_id":2,"repo":{"id":2,"owner":{"id":1,"login":"recovery-admin","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"recovery-admin@localhost.invalid","avatar_url":"http://127.0.0.1:3001/avatars/6e6d223f2e772760db23e0a961d67ab6","html_url":"http://127.0.0.