tent (#175)","body":"## Outcome and task contract\n\n#175 / 116-A now records independent whole-round declaration intent and preserves it across authenticated submission, reload, snapshots, split persistence, archive history and declaration undo.\n\n- Accepted current baseline: `dev@049b5a5da0d7b38c09553ed8896206badc9541b3`.\n- Candidate: `f3e7a386e39eaa5f67bc027e1b1fbe35232eac6f`; tree `61e4e53e11873470d04a91395e707727e4335617`. Ordered parents: original implementation `5c6fe53516888927a77ba3825cdfbb16f841f814`, then accepted baseline `049b5a5da0d7b38c09553ed8896206badc9541b3`.\n- Builder: `01a0a42c-2ef5-7b53-be6f-5152f309bbe6`, branch `codex/175-combat-declaration-foundation`, worktree `/Users/vidarhald/.codex/worktrees/dc51/glantri-app-forgejo`.\n- Authorized Recorder-relayed #175 contract and named sources read. Assigned `glantri-builder` publication targets `dev`; no merge authority.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdditive `declaration.intent` contains independent primary/secondary selections, structured description/target/subject/comment/task reference slots, ordered relative-position intentions (first is highest priority), movement direction and facing. Omitted choices remain unset; explicit `pass`, empty relative intentions, and movement `none` remain distinct.\n\nExisting execution fields retain their established behavior. Intent does not generate attacks, movement, modifiers, task transitions or resolved outcomes. New recorded actions are not made mechanically available. No historical conversion, default Pass, UI/editor, carry-forward, B–E mechanics, Panel, production repository, database-schema or migration changes.\n\n## Ownership and integration\n\nDomain owns representation, structural agreement, snapshots and preservation; API owns request/authority/private projection; the typed web client transports intent. Production persistence already serializes the shared schema without changes.\n\nAll ten changed paths are within the #175 lease, including the focused authenticated API test and history projector/test. Integration remains with the Development Orchestrator after independent exact-head QA and protected checks. Approved #174 documentation is integrated in the accepted current baseline. The coordinator performed the authorized mechanical merge, independently verified by this Builder. The first-parent delta contains only `apps/web/e2e/blackboard.spec.ts` and `docs/rules/combat-declarations.md`. The ten product blobs and complete product patch relative to the new baseline are byte-for-byte identical to the original implementation relative to its original baseline `79f69153ba97e4b8b2f242febe3637e62f45e6e2`. No source repair or rebase occurred.\n\n## Rule and architecture basis\n\nApproved `docs/rules/combat-declarations.md` at immutable #183 input `8355bef053561bb77f6a57e1da3d647edf27704b`, sections 1–2 and 5–10, plus the bounded #175 foundation contract. The supplied document worktree's later HEAD contains identical document content.\n\nParent acknowledged the optional opaque `taskId` reference seam for C. It carries no timer, status, rolls or GM notes. Legacy `actionId`/`secondaryActionId` are existing execution inputs; simultaneously supplied differing recorded action IDs fail structural agreement. Omitted intent from older clients is preserved; explicit `{}` clears it. The parent confirmed that a whole-round intended target must not overwrite or be inferred from separate Phase 1/Phase 2 targets. Both remain independently preserved, with no new targeting rule.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Strict schemas for recorded intent and structured specifications, shared by declarations and snapshots.\n- Explicit request parsing, declaration forwarding (including GM review), and typed client payload.\n- Canonical intent captured in snapshots and recovered in owner/GM history panels even when older snapshot summaries omit it.\n- Opponent projections omit intent during and after declaration; strict inputs reject injected GM-only fields.\n- Focused domain, history, compatibility, authenticated API and real PostgreSQL regressions.\n\n## Verification and review evidence\n\nBuilder result: **READY FOR INDEPENDENT QA** at the candidate above. Independent QA is pending and must be dispatched separately.\n\nRefresh checks at `f3e7a386e39eaa5f67bc027e1b1fbe35232eac6f` PASS: exact tree/ordered-parent verification, ten identical product blobs, byte-identical product patch, exact approved-document blob, first-parent and current-base whitespace, prerequisite formatting, Blackboard test lint, and 373 focused regression tests. No database resources were recreated. The refresh changed only previously integrated test/document prerequisites, so broad database/browser/full-suite reruns were not performed. Fresh independent QA must verify this rationale and choose appropriate new-head gates; no acceptance is reused.\n\nPrior implementation checks at `5c6fe53516888927a77ba3825cdfbb16f841f814` passed on Node 22.23.2 / pnpm 10.6.0 (retained evidence for unchanged product files, not newly executed checks at the refreshed head):\n\n- `pnpm typecheck` — 17/17 tasks; full `pnpm lint` — 11/11 tasks, plus final changed-source lint.\n- `pnpm test` — 11/11 tasks; database-dependent skips remain explicitly separate from the owned-database runs below.\n- `pnpm build` — 11/11 tasks, followed by final API build and dependency rebuilds through typecheck.\n- Final focused domain/history/compatibility/API conformance/persistence-comparison run — **373 tests passed**.\n- Authenticated API regression — **1 end-to-end fixture test passed** through real Fastify handlers, session authentication, canonical Scenario services and PostgreSQL. Owner and GM read exact intent; opponent and unrelated Admin cannot read private fields. Closed player resubmission remains rejected; supported GM clear/reopen handles fresh unset/zero-intent submissions. Privacy is also checked after the declaration step. This is HTTP injection evidence, not browser certification.\n- PostgreSQL split persistence suite — **3 tests passed**, including exact active/archive intent and reload → edit → persist → undo → persist preservation.\n- Changed-file Prettier and `git diff --check` pass; generated output is excluded.\n\nOwned PostgreSQL 16: `issue-175-dc51`, container `glantri-task-issue-175-dc51-pg16`, `127.0.0.1:61761`, databases `glantri_task_issue_175_dc51` and `glantri_task_issue_175_dc51_test`. Ownership/version verified; committed migrations applied to both. Cleanup passed: the exact owned container, anonymous volumes and `.env.task` were removed. No shared/persistent target was accessed.\n\nFunctional/mechanical examples cover explicit Pass versus unset, zero and multiple prioritized intentions, contradictory spatial intentions, independent movement/facing and action/Observe/relative targets, distinct phase contexts, structured comments/task references, archive and undo, and no inferred mechanics. No UI changed, so browser/responsive/accessibility checks are not applicable to this foundation slice.\n\nNew hosted checks are required for refreshed head `f3e7a386e39eaa5f67bc027e1b1fbe35232eac6f`; earlier-head runs #472/#473 cannot establish its gate status. Hosted protected checks are separate from local evidence and must pass before integration. No hosted PASS or acceptance is claimed here.\n\n## Handoff and authority checklist\n\n- [x] Scope matches #175; no unrelated fixes or Panel changes.\n- [x] Exact baseline and candidate are traceable; reservations and dependency order coordinated.\n- [x] Recorded intent versus legacy execution boundary and C task seam confirmed by parent.\n- [x] Verification and privacy evidence recorded; no synthetic substitute for authenticated/DB proof.\n- [x] Independent QA remains a fresh separate visible task, with no Builder acceptance claim.\n- [x] No main/production/Azure or deployment changes or authority.\n\n## Remaining risks and follow-ups\n\nIndependent QA and hosted gates are pending. B–E must expli